core_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.012520316748293181,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.4104012478344708,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":31.6,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.8272498831190083,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.0012190641677866515,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":32.9,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.029984187269050597,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.4,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.022991696020260233,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":61.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.0030399999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Savers Value Village, Inc., a thrift operator, sells second-hand merchandise in retail stores in the United States, Canada, and Australia. It purchases secondhand textiles, including clothing, bedding, and bath items; shoes; accessories; housewares; books; and other goods from non-profit partners and then processes, selects, prices, merchandises, and sells them in its stores. The company operates stores under the Savers, Value Village, Value Village Boutique, Village des Valeurs, Unique, and 2nd Avenue brands. It serves retail and wholesale customers. The company was formerly known as S-Evergreen Holding LLC and changed its name to Savers Value Village, Inc. in January 2022. Savers Value Village, Inc. was founded in 1954 and is based in Bellevue, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark T. Walsh | CEO, President & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 24K people. Revenue per employee of $70K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $2K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Savers Value Village, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.5B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 29%.","The business throws off $49M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 80% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8006176891369421},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.0pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $476.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 64/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Savers Value Village (NYSE:SVV) Announces FY 2026 Earnings Guidance","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/savers-value-village-nysesvv-announces-fy-2026-earnings-guidance.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793987816.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.893,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Savers Value Village (NYSE:SVV) Stock Price Up 13.4% After Better-Than-Expected Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/sa